{
  "configuration_id": "config_013",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only models (0.485–0.653) massively outperform the single image-only test (config_010, resnet50, 0.208). The image modality appears very weak, but we cannot yet tell whether this is because the image modality carries no useful signal or because resnet50 is a poor encoder for this task. Question: config_013 (image_only, ViT-L, singleprofile) isolates the image-encoder variable by swapping resnet50 → imagenet_vit_l while keeping everything else identical to config_010. If ViT-L also yields ~0.2 accuracy, the image modality is fundamentally uninformative and multimodal fusion is unlikely to add value, freeing budget for RNA-encoder refinement (e.g., scgpt). If ViT-L substantially improves, the image modality has recoverable signal and multimodal experiments become a high-priority direction. This single-variable comparison is the most informative use of the next experiment because it resolves the critical uncertainty about whether to invest remaining budget in multimodal fusion or to focus exclusively on optimizing the RNA pathway."
}

